-- title:
--   Every accepted quotient tuple is accepted by the legacy predicate after decoding
-- statement:
--   A statement of the module `MIPRE.Foundations.Introspection.TypedQuotientPredicate` of the MIP\* = RE formalization (commit `70cbf1c` of vidick/MIPRE-formalization). Quotient hiding comparisons in the complete typed predicate. The quotient comparisons accept every legacy accepted tuple. Deterministic answer decoding restores legacy acceptance on every raw question and answer, including consistency loops and both orientations of auxiliary edges.
--
--   Every accepted quotient tuple is accepted by the legacy predicate after decoding.
--   This statement covers every raw answer, rather than only sampler outputs.
--
--   **Formal statement.** In Lean, with the scope shown:
--
--   ```lean
--   open MIPRE
--   open MIPRE.Introspection
--   open MIPRE.Introspection.AuxiliaryQuotient
--   open Classical
--   variable {PauliType PauliAnswer F A : Type*} [Field F] {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] {ℓ : ℕ}
--   variable (L : Bool → CL.CLFun F (ι) ℓ) (X Z : PauliType)
--
--   theorem MIPRE.Introspection.AuxiliaryQuotient.check_sound (hL : ∀ w, (L w).SupportedOn Finset.univ)
--       (DP : PauliType → PauliType → PauliAnswer → PauliAnswer → Bool)
--       (t u : QuestionType PauliType ℓ) (a b : ParsedAnswer (ι → F) A PauliAnswer)
--       (h : check L X Z project D DP t u a b = true) :
--       TypedPredicate.check L X Z project D DP t u (decodeAnswer L t a) (decodeAnswer L u b) =
--         true
--   ```
--
--   **Formalization Note** `MIPRE.Introspection.AuxiliaryQuotient.check_sound` is declared in `MIPRE/Foundations/Introspection/TypedQuotientPredicate.lean`, lines 123–142. The binders, hypotheses and conclusion are exactly those of the Lean statement above; the uploaded statement elaborates to the same type as the declaration in the repository. The definitions it mentions are those of the published definition bundles of the module's import closure.
